  "fields": {
    "title": "Developer Tools",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The Developer tools make it possible to see the structure of any page on the web. Some of the main components of a web page are its basic structure (",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "5E1SmovXET5h0cV1E0tOzT",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "HTML",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "), its appearance (",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "3TBGoqMl1snjRBxLIzrc6Z",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "CSS",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ") and its functionality (JavaScript). All these files and elements can be viewed and temporarily manipulated via the DevTools. This makes it possible for everyone to see and test not only areas of an application that are visible in the browser, but also those that are hidden and cannot be seen via the frontend.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The fact that the source code of any website is available for anyone to see is a great feature of the web and at the same time a big difference to print media. Unlike books, where information about their design, such as the names of the fonts used or the baseline grid, and production, which papers were used, for example, is rarely comprehensible to viewers (except for some information in the masthead). ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Usage",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "You can find the Dev tools by clicking on the three dots at the top right, then selecting »",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "More tools«",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " and then »",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Developer tools«",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". Or you can just right click anywhere on a webpage and then select »",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Developer tool",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "s«. This works for Google Chrome and Safari.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "As soon as you open the Developer Console, a window opens next to the open browser page where you can find the following tools: ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Elements, Console, Memory, Sources, Network, Performance, Application, Security and Lighthouse",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Elements",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " usually opens first. It is very practical to use this function of the DevTools to inspect the attributes of HTML elements such as classes and IDs or the styling of individual elements, which can then be used for specific tests. This is particularly useful for test automation, where the elements to be tested are identified and controlled on the basis of selectors or specific values. But of course it's also quite useful to see the structure of a HTML document and to find out if (and which) ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6JvYGsB3Z0POfT9EnP867B",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "frameworks",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " were used to build the page. The styling of the page and specific elements can also be inspected, which is great for webdesigners. Also the ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "2ABYnMzPbdcoVRHCQpEav8",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "responsivness ",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "of the website can be tested by clicking on the smartphone",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "/tablet icon on the top left.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
